  "email": "sofia.rossi@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports not receiving Q4 planning meeting invite; need account, devices, and delegate context per KB-012."
}

{
  "email": "sofia.rossi@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-012 quick check: external or bulk calendar invites may be quarantined for the ticket sender."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, I checked your mailbox and nothing was held in quarantine, so the invite wasn't blocked as spam. To narrow this down, could you tell us two things: 1) Do you see the Q4 planning meeting when you open Outlook on the web (outlook.office.com)? If it shows there but not in the desktop app, we can walk through the Outlook sync steps. 2) Does anyone, such as an assistant, manage your calendar or receive invites on your behalf? Also, if it still doesn't appear, you can ask the meeting organizer to resend the invite to you directly. Reply to this ticket with what you find.",
  "internal_note": "Checked sofia.rossi (user_id 7, Marketing Coordinator, active, not locked, not blocked, mailbox 27.9% used, device BL-LT-0107). Spam quarantine for her mailbox is empty, so KB-007 release is not applicable. Lookup does not show delegate settings, so delegate status is unverified (KB-012 step 2). OWA vs desktop comparison (KB-012 step 3) requires user input. Next steps for user: confirm OWA view, confirm delegate status, and ask organizer to resend. If the invite is absent from OWA and no delegate exists, and the organizer is an internal user whose invites never arrive, escalate per KB-012 escalate-when. No actions were queued.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-012"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
